    "ui.intro_eyebrow": "Wanli 21 (1593), 1st month · The Ming army's eastern campaign",
    "ui.intro_body": "After retaking Pyongyang, Commander Li Rusong led a vanguard of mostly Liaodong cavalry south toward Hanseong and met the Japanese army near Byeokjegwan. Tachibana Muneshige's vanguard is already drawn up ahead, and Kobayakawa Takakage's main army is close behind. Li Rusong rode ahead with only half his guard; Yang Yuan follows with the other half.",
    "ui.tips_title": "Cavalry essentials",
    "ui.tip.1": "A charge needs a run-up: the faster you hit, the harder the impact. Fire the three-eyed guns before contact.",
    "ui.tip.2": "Flank ×1.8, rear ×2.4, and more against a wavering enemy. A big enough impact breaks the line.",
    "ui.tip.3": "Charging pikes head-on is costly. Teppō must halt and deploy to fire; hit them while they reload or march.",
    "ui.tip.4": "Re-forming after a charge takes about 48 s, and a long melee wears you down: break off and charge again. Cavalry pursue after a breakthrough, so recall them.",
    "ui.tip.5": "A broken unit scatters into two or three bands that flee apart, so you can hunt them separately; rallied remnants of the same camp merge when they meet.",
    "ui.tip.6": "Split: divide a unit into two halves, one to pin and one to flank. Detachments hit softer and cap lower in morale; Join them back together.",
    "ui.tip.7": "If Li Rusong falls, the battle is lost. Once the main army arrives, withdraw to Paju through the north exit; in a crisis Yang Yuan's horsemen will come.",
